  {
    "id": "2099996390218993769",
    "text": "The interesting thing about the Saudi east-to-west pipeline outage is that the Bab Al-Mandeb closure (by the Houthis) sent Saudi crude oil to the US before going to Asia. \n\nUS crude imports have been elevated because of this change in flow dynamics. \n\nNow that the outage is here and the Saudis are embracing the shuttle trade and getting the oil to Asia, the US is going to get sucked dry. \n\nTrump will have to announce another SPR release or US commercial crude storage will hit operational minimums by mid-November.",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-15T22:58:50+00:00",
    "tweetTime": 1789513130000,
    "username": "HFI_Research",
